n't that interested  in it anymore i wanted to run  my own thing  did you know wait but evan hold on did  you know when you have that instinct  because i think a lot of people have  that instinct of like i'm done with this  but did you know what the thing was that  you actually wanted to do  well i'm confused because you said you  were already doing it you said you were  already doing it and you were doing it  sucky  i didn't have 20 years of corporate  experience i never actually had a really  you know full-time job before starting  my company  but i thought i was going to be a banker  you looked at like when i graduated i  said i was going to be a banker and in  20 years to be the head of a investment  banking company that was my dream  growing up i didn't have an  entrepreneurial  you know family parents anything there's  no support network but when i started  doing this even like a taste it was part  time in university  something felt right like i had to keep  doing this like i felt  i owed it to myself like i could always  go what was your first entrepreneurial  venture what did you actually start out  doing  well i had a ton of like early failures  uh tiny small businesses like selling  baseball cards that kind of stuff the  very first thing i did was i i was five  and i encouraged my three-year-old  sister to drop pictures with me with my  door-to-door selling them and i earned  my first five cents on my neighbor  but the first real business was it was a  biotech software company and i i didn't  know anything about software i didn't  know anything about  biology uh but i came on and was  basically the business guy and helped  turn that off if you can't hold on a  second but if you came on you mean  somebody else had already started this  company and you came on or this was your  idea  no it was not my idea there were two  founders they had they had started the  company on their own two years prior  released a product that that was great  but  they just didn't know how to market  themselves and then are you a sales guy  or an entrepreneur because a salesman is  the guy who sells and makes other  people's ideas  fabulous and an entrepreneur is the guy  well they're not mutually exclusive but  i have that talent i want to know if  evans when you say you you were an  entrepreneur i don't consider you know  coming into somebody else's business and  making it successful you know you did  that somebody who builds a business  it's not just having a product you gotta  build up a business and part of that is  sales part of that's bringing on the  team and part of that's doing the media  yep yep they had a product that was a  good product but they didn't know  anything about building the business  that's what i came in got it how did you  know how to build a business i didn't  and i sucked at it  but i was interested for me and i was  passionate about it and i almost quit  multiple times like  this wasn't oh here's the answers and go  ahead and we were in some success  so how did it change for you so tell us  the moment when things started getting  traction and started to change for you  the moment changed when i i was at my  absolute lowest i i i was crying on the  phone with my partner and told him i  quit like i'm done this is too much  stress and work we're not gonna make it  uh and then the next day i woke up and i  and i realized i'm not the first guy to  try to solve this problem and that was  the challenge i had was i was trying to  do everything myself come with every  idea of myself i realized i'm not the  first guy and so i looked at other  software companies i looked at how bill  gates started microsoft and how intuit  started mac if you got started and i  looked at how they went from zero to one  not how bill gates makes an extra  million dollars now not interesting but  zero to one that's what i wanted to do  and i modeled his strategies and put it  to work for my business and we started  getting traction so so that 